  "paraphrase": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, who claims to have psychic abilities and is the daughter of one of Europe's most enduring royal leaders, married Durek Verrett, a Californian who identifies as a shaman with six generations of spiritual heritage. The Saturday afternoon nuptials were unconventional by royal standards, yet crowds gathered along the cloudy streets of Geiranger hoping to see the bride. At 52 years old, Märtha Louise holds fourth place in Norway's succession line as the sole daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja. The ceremony, following Church of Norway traditions, took place at the Hotel Union, a four-star establishment in a small community near the Geiranger fjord, with an audience of nobility and famous personalities. The 49-year-old groom saw his bride accompanied by seven attendants, among them her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her previous union with deceased Norwegian writer Ari Behn, which ended in divorce in 2017. Approximately 350 guests were present, including her sibling Crown Prince Haakon with Crown Princess Mette-Marit, Swedish royals Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel, plus Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien from the Netherlands. The princess has led an unorthodox royal existence, having claimed clairvoyant powers and operated a spiritual healing academy for ten years where she instructed students in angelic communication. In 2022, she revealed her decision to retire from formal royal responsibilities to concentrate on commercial ventures with Verrett and create clearer boundaries between their work and Norway's monarchy. On Instagram, Verrett presents himself as someone who serves God and activates energy. His clientele includes Gwyneth Paltrow, the Goop creator, whom he refers to as a spiritual sibling."
